Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["CyclicHochschildDifferential", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"e3b4ddf1-088e-48dc-867b-a468828978bd"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["CyclicHochschildDifferential"]], 
     "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CyclicHochschildDifferential", 
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["w", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["pairing", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c628eeaf-9ffd-40f4-82b3-e43917df0500"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the differential of the cyclic word ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ", induced particle by particle by the differential of the Poincare duality \
algebra that ",
 StyleBox["pairing", "TI"],
 " carries.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"a3d4b71e-8ffb-47fb-ac8d-b98d302f102e"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["CyclicHochschildDifferential"]], 
     "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CyclicHochschildDifferential", 
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["pairing", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "227d5750-5fc1-4f4b-8a34-76b355c26e09"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the extension of the differential as a derivation, applied to a \
product ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " of cyclic words."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"d044b19b-a325-4ef2-bbba-eb5570808785"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The differential is the operation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "0"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72bc5ff8-6571-43fb-b44b-a1dca6c420ca"],
 " of the dIBL structure of a cyclic cochain complex. It takes one cyclic \
word to a sum of cyclic words of the same length."
}], "Notes",
 CellFrameLabels->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {Inherited, 
    Cell[
     TextData[{
      "26.09.30: Design review - the differential is read from the \
\"Algebra\" key that GradedPairing[algebra] attaches, and from nothing else, \
so the alphabet is data: a pairing built by hand from degrees and values \
carries no algebra and every word is closed, with no message; no alternative \
was recorded. The sign is the running sign of the particles after the \
replaced one. It is the prefix rule of the literature read through the \
reversal sign $(-1)^{\\sum_{r<s}\\eta_r\\eta_s}$ that relates the cyclic \
words to the functionals of the literature; both give the same operation in \
different coordinates, and the sign is pinned by the Leibniz rule, as the \
statement that the differential kills the canonical Maurer-Cartan element. \
The function takes no \"EmptyWord\" option. Alternative name considered: \
CyclicDifferential, the name until 2026-09-30. Prior art: the Wolfram \
Language has no cyclic Hochschild complex; the verification suites pin the \
function on the two nilmanifold alphabets against their differential \
pairings, and check that it squares to zero, lowers the degree, anticommutes \
with the bracket and the co-bracket, and vanishes on an alphabet of the \
catalogue exactly when its quotient carries the differential 0.", "\n\n", 
       Cell[
        BoxData[
         GridBox[{{
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Edit"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationButton"]]], 
            StyleBox[
             RowBox[{
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "LastAnnotator"]], "pavel"}], 
             "TextAnnotator"], 
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Delete"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationRemoveButton"]]], ""}}, 
          GridBoxAlignment -> {
           "Columns" -> {Left, Left, Right, Right}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
          GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.68], 
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.02]}}]]], "\n"}], "TextAnnotation", 
     CellSize -> {590, Inherited}]}},
 CellTags->"TextAnnotation",
 CellID->335082183,ExpressionUUID->"751f6c61-5c00-42da-b76c-b4112f57617d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each particle in turn is replaced by its image under the differential dual \
to the one of the algebra, with the sign ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ")"}], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9bbb159e-ae7d-4a69-80df-4ac7d24c9fe4"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ffe55f67-3085-40bf-b02a-14c689253db8"],
 " being the bar degree of the particles after it."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8bc9a6c9-9e5f-4c1b-a453-f73c21359198"],

Cell["\<\
It lowers the degree by one, and it preserves the length of a word and the \
number of factors of a product.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d8b337b6-234d-4ff7-b3ec-20a0e0989701"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The differential is read from the ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Algebra\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b6b41781-5a12-4d5c-818f-2db1a4a622d0"],
 " key of ",
 StyleBox["pairing", "TI"],
 ", which ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["GradedPairing"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/GradedPairing", 
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["algebra", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55c57f58-43af-47ba-805a-acfc7491d9ab"],
 " attaches, for instance to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"GradedPairing", "[", 
   RowBox[{"NondegenerateQuotient", "[", "model", "]"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b930f6c-9341-49f5-b0b6-5b426e4ad692"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d89bfbcd-623f-4727-9125-d3d003e7f60b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A pairing built from degrees and pairing values carries no algebra, and the \
differential of every word is then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8cf83268-d4ee-4f91-bb08-7b2520e4926c"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"316e5bd5-c6fc-4c07-919c-99caf18216f4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The differential is also ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f47d0c48-b9a4-4e48-bbbf-4e0642abb341"],
 " when the Poincare duality algebra carries the differential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b467996-bcf6-451f-9645-b04d322ec056"],
 ", as the nondegenerate quotient of a formal model does. The alphabets of \
the non-formal models ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<HeisenbergNilmanifold\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ba33809e-afb8-4345-b7fa-70f29122b575"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<KodairaThurston\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77a09dd7-af80-430f-b345-256ae58e5d15"],
 " of the catalogue carry a nonzero differential."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ccb7e22a-431a-4eb1-a4c4-72c78bcf0a0f"],

Cell["\<\
On a cyclic word the operation carries no degree-shift sign, so it is the \
same in both pictures.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c635d08e-f3fb-417e-8ff9-5dbfbea8d27a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the second form the differential is applied to each factor of ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " in turn, with the Koszul sign of the shuffle that brings it to the front. \
The convention of ",
 StyleBox["pairing", "TI"],
 " selects the picture of the product."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"68dd7a1a-8ad3-430d-b87d-725bef107ec8"],

Cell["\<\
Both forms are linear: they distribute over sums and pull out scalars.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e9c17bd0-431d-49fc-9f5e-d29229d93908"],

Cell["A word may be given as the list of its particles.", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b9b957c5-9a90-4418-bbf1-0f3a88ccde21"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A product whose head disagrees with the convention of ",
 StyleBox["pairing", "TI"],
 " returns unevaluated."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8cdf90aa-550f-4996-a310-67f4e4167309"],

